n Mechanism of Mg(OH)2 Prepared by Hydration of Magnesia Clinker in Magnesium Salt Solution (PART 1)' NIPPON CERAMICS KYOKAI GAKUJUTSU RONBUNSHI, vol. 97, no. 7, 1989, (TOKYO), pages 683 - 689, XP002930101</text><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1063199A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ANDO TARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAISHI WATARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KYOWA CHEM IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OISHI SHUNJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHII MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANDO, TARO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAISHI, WATARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KYOWA CHEMICAL INDUSTRY CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OISHI, SHUNJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHII, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ANDO TARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAISHI WATARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OISHI SHUNJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHII MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ANDO, TARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAISHI, WATARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OISHI, SHUNJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHII, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Magnesium hydroxide particles having a hexagonal platy crystal form and an aspect ratio (H) satisfying the following relationship (I) 0.45.A.B&lt;H&lt;1.1.A.B, wherein H represents the aspect ratio; A represents the average secondary diameter of all the particles as determined by the laser diffraction scattering method ( mu m); and B represents the specific surface area of all the particles as determined by the BET method (m&lt;2&gt;/g)]; a flame retardant comprising the particles; a flame-retardant resin composition comprising 100 parts by weight of a synthetic resin and 5 to 300 parts by weight of the magnesium hydroxide particles; and a molded article obtained therefrom. The magnesium hydroxide particles are composed of single-crystal particles of a hexagonal platy form. Although the hexagonal shape need not be regular and the crystals need not have the same size, the particles have a specific aspect ratio in relation to the specific surface area and the average particle diameter. They have excellent properties when used as a flame retardant for synthetic resins.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des particules d'hydroxyde de magnésium ayant une forme de cristaux hexagonaux lamellaires et un facteur de forme (H) satisfaisant l'équation (I) 0.45.A.B&lt;H&lt;1.1.A.B, dans laquelle H représente le facteur de forme; A représente le diamètre secondaire moyen de la totalité des particules, tel que déterminé par le procédé ( mu m) de diffusion à diffraction laser; et B représente l'aire spécifique de la totalité des particules, telles que déterminée par le procédé BET (m&lt;2&gt;/g). L'invention concerne également un retardateur de flamme comprenant lesdites particules ; une composition de résine ignifuge comprenant 100 parties en poids de résine synthétique et de 5 à 300 parties en poids de particules d'hydroxyde de magnésium; ainsi qu'un article moulé obtenu à partir de ces particules. Les particules d'hydroxyde de magnésium sont composées de particules monocristallines de forme hexagonale lamellaire. Bien que la forme hexagonale n'ait pas besoin d'être régulière et que les cristaux ne doivent pas nécessairement avoir la même forme, les particules ont un facteur de forme spécifique par rapport à l'aire spécifique et au diamètre moyen des particules. Ces particules présentent d'excellentes propriétés lorsqu'on les utilise comme retardateurs de flamme pour des résines synthétiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>